# No v1 synth / harmonica UI in new work

When embedding or composing a keyboard, harmonica diagram, or scale lock
for **new** pages (lessons, genres, scales, labs), use the **v2**
components. Never reach for the v1 / `templates/basic-synth` UI just
because it is closer in the tree or already imported somewhere.

The 2026-09 blues-scale lesson did this: it wrapped v1 `SynthKeys` and
rebuilt lock + degree labels that `KeyboardV2` already had.

## Use these

| Need | Component |
|------|-----------|
| Playable piano / scale degrees / lock | `KeyboardV2` (`src/instruments/synth/v2/KeyboardV2.tsx`) |
| Full synth page chrome (don't embed the whole page) | `SynthV2` |
| Harmonica diagram | `HarmonicaDiagramV2` |
| Position / key matrix | `PositionMatrixV2` |
| Harmonica lab shell | `HarmonicaLabV2` |

Shared **non-UI** is fine to keep using: `useAudioSynthesis`,
`createSynthKeysFromRange` / `synthUtils`, `useSharedAudioContext`,
`src/lib/music`, `src/lib/harmonica` (the theory engine).

## Do not import for new work

- `src/instruments/synth/templates/basic-synth/components/**` — `SynthKeys`,
  `SynthKeyboard`, `SynthControls`, theory panels, `AudioPermissionOverlay`
- `src/instruments/synth/templates/basic-synth/hooks/useScaleLogic.ts` —
  major/minor only; new scale UI reads `src/lib/music/scales.ts`
- `src/components/harmonica/*.tsx` (the folder root, **not** `v2/`) —
  `HarmonicaDiagram`, `PositionMatrix`, `KeySelector`, `NoteCell`, etc.
- Barrel `src/components/harmonica/index.ts` and
  `src/instruments/synth/index.ts` (they re-export v1)

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — v1 keyboard, missing degrees + lock language
import SynthKeys from "@/instruments/synth/templates/basic-synth/components/SynthKeys";

// ✅ GOOD — same piano the live synth already shows
import { KeyboardV2 } from "@/instruments/synth/v2/KeyboardV2";
```

## If v2 is missing a prop

Extend the **v2** component (the way `scaleDegrees` now accepts `"♭5"`).
Do not fork v1 or add a third keyboard. Touch v1 only when the user
explicitly asks to change the legacy `/synth` or `/harmonica-lab` pages.
